  "id": "empathy-altruism-hypothesis",
  "term": "empathy-altruism hypothesis",
  "definition": "The empathy-altruism hypothesis is the idea that empathy toward other people is a necessary basis for altruistic behavior. In plain terms, it proposes that feeling or understanding another person’s emotions helps motivate actions intended to benefit them.",
